<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fourah Bay College</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1827">1827</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fourah Bay College is a college in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freetown">Freetown</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a>, founded by the Church Missionary Society in 1827, the first Western-style institution of higher learning in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>. Affiliated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durham-university">Durham University</a> from 1876, it trained clergy, teachers and clerks for much of British West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, earning Freetown the name &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> of West Africa&quot;. It is now part of the University of Sierra Leone.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fourah-bay-college.jpg" alt="Fourah Bay College" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AlexD~commonswiki · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fourah_Bay_College_shield.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
